.page md5sum 1 compute and check MD5 message digests

# SYNOPSIS
*md5sum* [*-b*] [_FILE_...]
*md5sum* *-c* [_LISTFILE_]

# DESCRIPTION
`md5sum` prints the MD5 digest of each _FILE_ as 32 hexadecimal digits, two spaces and the file name. With no file it reads standard input and prints `-` as the name. MD5 is good for spotting accidental changes and bad against someone who wants to fool you; for that use sha256sum(1).

# OPTIONS
@ *-c*
    Check: read lines of the form written by `md5sum` from _LISTFILE_ (or standard input) and verify each named file. Each file is reported as `NAME: OK` or `NAME: FAILED`; a file that cannot be opened is `FAILED open or read`.
@ *-b*
    Accepted for compatibility; there is no difference.

# EXIT STATUS
0 if all went well, 1 if a file was unreadable or a check failed.

# EXAMPLES
    echo -n abc | md5sum
    md5sum /bin/gapsh > /tmp/sums
    md5sum -c /tmp/sums

# SEE ALSO
sha256sum(1), crc32(1), cmp(1)
